# Copy to .env (gitignored) and adjust for your setup.
# 10.0.2.2 is the Android emulator's alias for the host machine's localhost —
# use it when admill-backend runs on the same dev machine as the emulator.
# A physical device needs the host machine's real LAN IP instead.
API_BASE_URL=http://10.0.2.2:5000/api/v1
SOCKET_URL=http://10.0.2.2:5000

# Required — every map screen (Owner Live Fleet Tracking, Customer Fare
# Estimate/tracking) renders a solid black screen on Android without a real
# key (confirmed on a real device — not a graceful no-tiles fallback). Get
# one at https://console.cloud.google.com/google/maps-apis — enable "Maps
# SDK for Android", create an API key. Restrict it to this app's package
# name (com.admillmobile) + your signing certificate's SHA-1
# (`gradlew signingReport` in android/) to prevent misuse if leaked.
#
# ALSO used from JS for route-line rendering (src/utils/directions.ts,
# Phase 5 Polyline) — calls the Routes API (routes.googleapis.com). This
# needs the Routes API enabled on the same Cloud project (separate from
# "Maps SDK for Android"), and the package/SHA-1 restriction above does NOT
# authorize this call (that restriction type only applies to the native
# Maps SDK's own requests, not a plain fetch()) — a real key with Routes API
# enabled + a Cloud Console daily quota cap is required for polylines to
# actually render. Without it, getRoute() fails safe: the map still works,
# just markers-only, exactly like before this feature existed.
GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=
